1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,408 --> 00:00:04,334
Hi!

3
00:00:04,384 --> 00:00:06,412
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,534 --> 00:00:11,765
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,076 --> 00:00:15,503
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,553 --> 00:00:18,427
Rapunzel and the Tower in the Woods!

7
00:00:23,006 --> 00:00:27,262
Once upon a time, in a quiet
village near the forest,

8
00:00:27,312 --> 00:00:32,067
there lived a husband and a wife who
were waiting for a baby with lots of

9
00:00:32,117 --> 00:00:33,317
love.

10
00:00:33,747 --> 00:00:38,030
Their house was small, but from the
back window they could see an enormous

11
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:41,800
garden, surrounded by a very tall wall.

12
00:00:42,442 --> 00:00:45,851
That garden was full of
flowers, fruit and vegetables,

13
00:00:45,901 --> 00:00:50,884
and it belonged to a very powerful
and very grumpy enchantress.

14
00:00:51,533 --> 00:00:55,803
Nobody in the village dared to go
into that garden, because everyone was

15
00:00:55,853 --> 00:00:58,114
afraid of the enchantress.

16
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:02,830
One day, the wife saw a patch
of rampion in the garden,

17
00:01:02,903 --> 00:01:07,164
a vegetable with green leaves
that in German is called rapunzel.

18
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:11,953
Oh, I would so love a salad of those
green leaves, I think only that would

19
00:01:12,003 --> 00:01:13,329
make me feel better,

20
00:01:13,379 --> 00:01:15,876
the wife said, looking out of the window.

21
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:21,762
The husband loved his wife so much
that, at dusk, he climbed over the tall

22
00:01:21,812 --> 00:01:25,615
wall and picked a handful
of leaves without asking.

23
00:01:28,512 --> 00:01:33,287
The wife loved the salad, and the next
day she wanted to eat even more of it.

24
00:01:33,915 --> 00:01:38,476
So the husband climbed over the wall
once again, but when he landed on the

25
00:01:38,526 --> 00:01:42,829
ground, the enchantress was
standing right in front of him.

26
00:01:43,899 --> 00:01:48,281
How dare you come into my garden
and take my plants without asking?

27
00:01:48,331 --> 00:01:51,092
the enchantress asked, very cross.

28
00:01:51,643 --> 00:01:56,633
I am so sorry, madam, my wife is expecting
a baby, and she wanted those green

29
00:01:56,683 --> 00:01:58,331
leaves so very much,

30
00:01:58,381 --> 00:02:01,725
the husband answered, trembling with fear.

31
00:02:02,336 --> 00:02:06,578
The enchantress let the husband
take as many leaves as he wanted,

32
00:02:06,628 --> 00:02:09,473
but she made a very serious deal.

33
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:13,696
When the baby is born, the child
will come and live with me,

34
00:02:13,746 --> 00:02:17,371
and I promise to look after her
with all the care in the world,

35
00:02:17,421 --> 00:02:20,238
the enchantress said in a firm voice.

36
00:02:20,888 --> 00:02:25,727
The husband was so frightened that he
said yes, and he went back home with a

37
00:02:25,777 --> 00:02:27,079
heavy heart.

38
00:02:27,716 --> 00:02:33,644
Soon after, a lovely baby girl was born,
and the enchantress came to take her,

39
00:02:33,758 --> 00:02:35,603
just as they had agreed.

40
00:02:36,252 --> 00:02:40,507
She named the girl Rapunzel, just like
the vegetable with green leaves from

41
00:02:40,557 --> 00:02:41,757
the garden.

42
00:02:42,147 --> 00:02:46,666
The parents were very sad, but they
kept in their hearts the hope of finding

43
00:02:46,716 --> 00:02:48,880
their daughter again one day.

44
00:02:49,982 --> 00:02:53,632
Rapunzel grew up to be the
loveliest girl in the kingdom,

45
00:02:53,690 --> 00:02:57,687
with long golden hair that
shone like threads of gold.

46
00:02:58,302 --> 00:03:03,349
When she turned twelve, the enchantress
took her to a very tall tower in the

47
00:03:03,399 --> 00:03:05,160
middle of the forest.

48
00:03:05,790 --> 00:03:10,990
The tower had no door and no stairs,
and at the very top there was only one

49
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:13,884
small window, where you could see the sky.

50
00:03:14,541 --> 00:03:19,325
Whenever the enchantress wanted to go
up, she stood at the bottom and called

51
00:03:19,375 --> 00:03:20,622
out loudly.

52
00:03:21,236 --> 00:03:24,862
Rapunzel, Rapunzel, let
down your hair to me!

53
00:03:24,912 --> 00:03:28,465
the enchantress called,
at the foot of the tower.

54
00:03:29,072 --> 00:03:32,828
Then Rapunzel let her long
braid down from the window,

55
00:03:32,878 --> 00:03:36,584
and the enchantress climbed
up it, as if it were a rope.

56
00:03:37,242 --> 00:03:40,817
The days in the tower were
calm and a little lonely,

57
00:03:40,867 --> 00:03:44,781
and Rapunzel spent the hours
singing beautiful songs.

58
00:03:45,388 --> 00:03:50,796
One afternoon, a brown owl with a red
bow on her head landed on the tower

59
00:03:50,846 --> 00:03:52,046
window.

60
00:03:52,370 --> 00:03:53,747
Hoo, hoo!

61
00:03:53,853 --> 00:03:58,673
What a lovely voice you have, I am
Popcorn and I would really like to be your

62
00:03:58,723 --> 00:03:59,518
friend,

63
00:03:59,568 --> 00:04:02,843
Popcorn said, blinking her big eyes.

64
00:04:03,507 --> 00:04:08,540
From then on, Popcorn came every afternoon
to tell Rapunzel the news from the

65
00:04:08,590 --> 00:04:11,796
forest, the river and the village.

66
00:04:18,875 --> 00:04:23,414
A few years later, a prince rode
his horse through the forest.

67
00:04:28,441 --> 00:04:33,738
Suddenly, he heard a voice singing, so
sweetly that he stopped his horse to

68
00:04:33,788 --> 00:04:34,988
listen.

69
00:04:35,328 --> 00:04:39,834
The prince looked for a door in the
tower, but he could not find one,

70
00:04:39,884 --> 00:04:42,881
and he rode home thinking about that song.

71
00:04:43,538 --> 00:04:49,238
The next day, hiding behind a tree, he
saw the enchantress call Rapunzel and

72
00:04:49,288 --> 00:04:51,396
climb up the golden braid.

73
00:04:52,021 --> 00:04:56,527
When the enchantress had gone away,
the prince came close to the tower and

74
00:04:56,577 --> 00:04:59,213
called out in the very same way.

75
00:04:59,856 --> 00:05:02,923
Rapunzel, Rapunzel, let
down your hair to me!

76
00:05:02,973 --> 00:05:06,554
the prince called, with
his heart beating fast.

77
00:05:07,192 --> 00:05:11,962
The golden braid came down the wall,
and the prince carefully climbed all the

78
00:05:12,012 --> 00:05:14,092
way up to the tower window.

79
00:05:14,752 --> 00:05:19,868
Rapunzel got a big surprise, because
she had never seen a young man in her

80
00:05:19,918 --> 00:05:21,193
whole life.

81
00:05:21,921 --> 00:05:26,288
But the prince spoke very gently, and
soon the two of them were chatting like

82
00:05:26,338 --> 00:05:27,682
old friends.

83
00:05:28,311 --> 00:05:32,074
I heard you singing from the forest,
and your voice made me happy all day

84
00:05:32,124 --> 00:05:32,795
long,

85
00:05:32,845 --> 00:05:34,981
the prince said with a smile.

86
00:05:36,077 --> 00:05:40,935
From that day on, the prince came
to visit Rapunzel every afternoon,

87
00:05:41,091 --> 00:05:43,588
after the enchantress had gone away.

88
00:05:44,241 --> 00:05:48,413
Rapunzel really wanted to see the world
outside, and the two of them had a

89
00:05:48,463 --> 00:05:50,418
very clever idea.

90
00:05:51,062 --> 00:05:55,736
Every time you come, please bring a
skein of silk, and I will weave a ladder

91
00:05:55,786 --> 00:05:57,511
to climb down from the tower,

92
00:05:57,561 --> 00:05:59,780
Rapunzel asked excitedly.

93
00:06:00,433 --> 00:06:04,633
Popcorn helped hold the threads with
her beak, and the silk ladder grew a

94
00:06:04,683 --> 00:06:07,166
little longer every afternoon.

95
00:06:07,819 --> 00:06:12,450
But one day, Rapunzel was not paying
attention and said something without

96
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:13,700
thinking.

97
00:06:14,130 --> 00:06:17,900
Why is it that you are so much
heavier to pull up than the prince?

98
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:20,225
Rapunzel asked, by accident.

99
00:06:20,845 --> 00:06:25,518
The enchantress was so cross that she
took a big pair of scissors and cut off

100
00:06:25,568 --> 00:06:27,579
Rapunzel's long braid.

101
00:06:29,386 --> 00:06:34,378
Then she took Rapunzel to a faraway
valley, on the other side of the forest,

102
00:06:34,428 --> 00:06:37,356
where she would have to
live far from everyone.

103
00:06:37,999 --> 00:06:42,976
But Popcorn flew after them, so that
Rapunzel would never be without a friend

104
00:06:43,026 --> 00:06:44,226
nearby.

105
00:06:45,148 --> 00:06:49,682
That afternoon, the prince arrived
at the tower and called Rapunzel,

106
00:06:49,732 --> 00:06:51,534
just as he always did.

107
00:06:52,211 --> 00:06:55,383
The enchantress had tied
the cut braid to the window,

108
00:06:55,433 --> 00:06:56,931
and she let it down.

109
00:06:57,583 --> 00:07:02,311
When the prince reached the top, the
one waiting for him was the enchantress,

110
00:07:02,361 --> 00:07:04,691
with a very cross face.

111
00:07:05,309 --> 00:07:09,481
Your friend does not live here anymore,
and you will never find Rapunzel

112
00:07:09,531 --> 00:07:10,328
again,

113
00:07:10,378 --> 00:07:13,598
the enchantress said, folding her arms.

114
00:07:14,211 --> 00:07:19,147
The prince was so startled that he slid
down the braid and landed in a very

115
00:07:19,197 --> 00:07:21,930
soft bush, without getting hurt.

116
00:07:22,548 --> 00:07:27,415
But he was so sad that he lost his way
home, and for many days he wandered

117
00:07:27,465 --> 00:07:31,170
through the forest, looking
for Rapunzel everywhere.

118
00:07:32,261 --> 00:07:36,953
In the faraway valley, Rapunzel
lived in a simple wooden cabin,

119
00:07:37,192 --> 00:07:39,855
next to a stream of clear water.

120
00:07:40,499 --> 00:07:45,246
She missed her friend very much,
but every morning she still sang,

121
00:07:45,305 --> 00:07:48,024
so that the day would
begin more cheerfully.

122
00:07:48,676 --> 00:07:53,543
Meanwhile, Popcorn flew over the forest,
searching for the prince with her

123
00:07:53,593 --> 00:07:55,895
big, watchful eyes.

124
00:07:56,473 --> 00:07:57,849
Hoo, hoo!

125
00:07:57,956 --> 00:08:03,773
I found you, prince, come with me,
because I know where Rapunzel lives now,

126
00:08:03,823 --> 00:08:06,820
Popcorn said, flying ahead of him.

127
00:08:11,911 --> 00:08:15,431
The prince followed the owl
over mountains and rivers,

128
00:08:15,481 --> 00:08:19,603
until he heard that sweet voice
singing again in the distance.

129
00:08:20,231 --> 00:08:24,135
Rapunzel, I have searched for you
in every corner of the forest,

130
00:08:24,185 --> 00:08:26,414
and at last I have found your voice!

131
00:08:26,464 --> 00:08:29,087
the prince said, full of emotion.

132
00:08:29,741 --> 00:08:34,663
Rapunzel ran to hug her friend, and their
happy tears fell on the grass of the

133
00:08:34,713 --> 00:08:35,913
valley.

134
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:41,091
The prince took Rapunzel back to the
village, and Popcorn showed them the way

135
00:08:41,141 --> 00:08:43,568
to the stone house next to the garden.

136
00:08:44,213 --> 00:08:48,030
When the mother and father saw
that young woman with golden hair,

137
00:08:48,144 --> 00:08:52,025
they recognized their daughter
at once and gave her a big,

138
00:08:52,075 --> 00:08:53,275
tight hug.

139
00:08:53,766 --> 00:08:57,998
We waited for you every single day, our
daughter, and we never stopped loving

140
00:08:58,048 --> 00:08:58,600
you,

141
00:08:58,650 --> 00:09:01,369
the mother said, crying with joy.

142
00:09:02,015 --> 00:09:05,846
That night, the enchantress
appeared at the garden gate,

143
00:09:06,001 --> 00:09:11,026
alone and very quiet, holding
a basket of green leaves.

144
00:09:11,646 --> 00:09:16,499
I wanted to keep you all to myself, but
now I understand that true love never

145
00:09:16,549 --> 00:09:18,093
locks anyone away,

146
00:09:18,143 --> 00:09:20,571
the enchantress said, ashamed.

147
00:09:21,216 --> 00:09:26,095
I forgive you, and the gate of this
house will always be open for a visit,

148
00:09:26,145 --> 00:09:29,087
Rapunzel answered with a kind smile.

149
00:09:29,741 --> 00:09:33,905
From then on, the enchantress
left the garden gate open,

150
00:09:33,978 --> 00:09:38,108
and everyone in the village could pick
flowers and vegetables whenever they

151
00:09:38,158 --> 00:09:39,358
liked.

152
00:09:39,710 --> 00:09:44,410
Soon after, Rapunzel and the prince
had a wedding party in the garden,

153
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:47,540
full of flowers, music, and cake.

154
00:09:48,221 --> 00:09:52,435
Popcorn landed on the garden
wall, straightened her red bow,

155
00:09:52,485 --> 00:09:55,288
and watched the party, full of joy.

156
00:09:55,903 --> 00:09:57,280
Hoo, hoo!

157
00:09:57,396 --> 00:10:02,294
True love never locks anyone
away, it cares, it trusts,

158
00:10:02,344 --> 00:10:03,970
and it lets us fly,

159
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:07,420
Popcorn said in her soft and sweet voice.

160
00:10:08,060 --> 00:10:13,260
And Rapunzel lived happily ever after,
singing every morning for anyone who

161
00:10:13,310 --> 00:10:14,613
wanted to listen.

162
00:10:21,905 --> 00:10:23,105
The End.

163
00:10:24,812 --> 00:10:25,524
Hoo...

164
00:10:25,574 --> 00:10:26,599
Psst!

165
00:10:26,649 --> 00:10:28,221
Are you still awake?

166
00:10:28,375 --> 00:10:30,428
Did you like tonight's story?

167
00:10:30,546 --> 00:10:34,520
Rapunzel and Popcorn showed
us that true love cares,

168
00:10:34,570 --> 00:10:39,657
trusts, and lets us fly, and that
forgiving makes our hearts light.

169
00:10:39,861 --> 00:10:44,167
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

170
00:10:44,463 --> 00:10:49,361
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

171
00:10:49,411 --> 00:10:51,816
for more stories at bedtime.

172
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:53,320
Hoo...

